      "text": "To determine the cost of the gas used for the trip, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total distance traveled.\n2. Determine the amount of gas used.\n3. Calculate the cost of the gas used.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total distance traveled.**\nThe odometer reads 74,568 when Ryosuke picks up his friend and 74,592 when he drops his friend off at his house. The distance traveled is:\n\\[ 74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the amount of gas used.**\nRyosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon. Therefore, the amount of gas used for 24 miles is:\n\\[ \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the cost of the gas used.**\nThe price of one gallon of gas is $4.05. Therefore, the cost of \\(\\frac{6}{7}\\) gallons of gas is:\n\\[ \\frac{6}{7} \\times 4.05 = \\frac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} = \\frac{24.3}{7} = 3.47142857 \\approx 3.47 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the gas used for the trip is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3.47} \\]",
