      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total distance driven:**\n   The odometer reads 74,568 when Ryosuke picks up his friend and 74,592 when he drops his friend off. The distance driven is:\n   \\[\n   74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the amount of gasoline used:**\n   Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon. The amount of gasoline used for the 24-mile trip is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the cost of the gasoline used:**\n   The price of one gallon of gas is \\$4.05. The cost of \\(\\frac{6}{7}\\) gallons of gas is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6}{7} \\times 4.05 = \\frac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} = \\frac{24.3}{7} \\approx 3.4714\n   \\]\n   Rounding to the nearest cent, the cost is:\n   \\[\n   3.47\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the gas that was used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work is \\(\\boxed{3.47}\\).",
